{"id":"8ccdb4cc-20fa-4c56-a092-7af1b6c9acb5","object":"chat.completion","created":1784835439,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\n  \"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import math\\n\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    if not isinstance(case, dict):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must be a dictionary\\\")\\n    if 'threshold' not in case or 'calls' not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"case must contain 'threshold' and 'calls'\\\")\\n    threshold = case['threshold']\\n    if not isinstance(threshold, (int, float)):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"threshold must be numeric\\\")\\n    calls = case['calls']\\n    if not isinstance(calls, list):\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"calls must be a list\\\")\\n\\n    diagnostics = []\\n    accepted = []\\n\\n    for call in calls:\\n        if not isinstance(call, dict):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"each call must be a dictionary\\\")\\n        required = ['call_id', 'loss_without_call', 'loss_with_call', 'prediction_tokens', 'parseable']\\n        for field in required:\\n            if field not in call:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"call missing required field '{field}'\\\")\\n        call_id = call['call_id']\\n        loss_without = call['loss_without_call']\\n        loss_with = call['loss_with_call']\\n        pred_tokens = call['prediction_tokens']\\n        parseable = call['parseable']\\n\\n        if not isinstance(loss_without, (int, float)) or not isinstance(loss_with, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"loss values must be numeric\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(pred_tokens, int) or pred_tokens <= 0:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"prediction_tokens must be a positive integer\\\")\\n        if not isinstance(parseable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"parseable must be a boolean\\\")\\n\\n        gain = loss_without - loss_with\\n        normalized_gain = gain / pred_tokens\\n        is_accepted = parseable and normalized_gain >= threshold\\n\\n        diag = {\\n            'call_id': call_id,\\n            'loss_without_call': loss_without,\\n            'loss_with_call': loss_with,\\n            'gain': round(gain, 6),\\n            'normalized_gain': round(normalized_gain, 6),\\n            'parseable': parseable,\\n            'accepted': is_accepted\\n        }\\n        diagnostics.append(diag)\\n        if is_accepted:\\n            accepted.append(call_id)\\n\\n    return {\\n        'accepted': accepted,\\n        'diagnostics': diagnostics\\n    }\\n\"\n}","reasoning_content":"We need to implement `solve(case)` that processes the case payload with calls, threshold, etc. The output should be a JSON-serializable object. The objective: retain API-call candidates using normalized future-token weights, weighted losses, stronger counterfactual, inclusive threshold. \n\nInterpretation: For each call, compute gain = loss_without_call - loss_with_call. Then normalize gain by prediction_tokens? \"Normalize gain by at least one prediction token\" suggests dividing gain by prediction_tokens? But \"normalized future-token weights\" might mean per-token gain? Actually \"normalized gain by at least one prediction token\" could mean we compute normalized_gain = gain / prediction_tokens. But ensure at least one token? Probably if prediction_tokens is 0? But fixtures show positive integers.\n\nThen \"Require both parseability and normalized gain at or above threshold.\" So we filter calls where parseable is True and normalized_gain >= threshold.\n\n\"Return accepted call IDs and rounded per-call diagnostics.\" What diagnostics? Probably the computed fields: gain, normalized_gain, etc. Also \"stronger_counterfactual\" might be something else? The description: \"Implement api_call_loss_filter through solve(case) for this bounded objective: Retain API-call candidates using normalized future-token weights, weighted losses, the stronger counterfactual, and an inclu